{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(array1: list, array2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two arrays follow the same structural pattern.\n    This involves mapping elements to their first occurrence index.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array1) != len(array2):\n        return False\n\n    map1 = {}\n    map2 = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(array1)):\n        # If element from array1 is new, map it to its index.\n        # Otherwise, check if its previously mapped index matches map2's current index.\n        if array1[i] not in map1:\n            map1[array1[i]] = i\n        \n        # Similar logic for array2.\n        if array2[i] not in map2:\n            map2[array2[i]] = i\n        \n        # If the first occurrence index for corresponding elements doesn't match, patterns are different.\n        if map1[array1[i]] != map2[array2[i]]:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
