{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main function that counts odd decimal values from binary string rotations.\n    Counts how many of those decimal values are odd numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    def rotate_left(s: str, positions: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Rotates string left by specified positions.\"\"\"\n        effective_positions = positions % len(s)\n        return s[effective_positions:] + s[:effective_positions]\n\n    def binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts binary string to decimal integer.\"\"\"\n        return int(binary_str, 2)\n\n    def is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is odd.\"\"\"\n        return number % 2 != 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    n = len(binary_string)\n    for i in range(rotations):\n        rotated_string = rotate_left(binary_string, i)\n        decimal_value = binary_to_decimal(rotated_string)\n        if is_odd(decimal_value):\n            odd_count += 1\n    return odd_count"}
