{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(upper_limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sums all amicable numbers up to the specified upper_limit.\n    An amicable pair (a, b) consists of two different numbers such that\n    the sum of the proper divisors of a is b, and the sum of the proper\n    divisors of b is a.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def sum_of_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given number.\n        Proper divisors are positive divisors excluding the number itself.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return 0\n        s = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor for n > 1\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                s += i\n                if i * i != n:\n                    s += n // i\n        return s\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for num in range(1, upper_limit + 1):\n        if num in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        sum1 = sum_of_divisors(num)\n\n        # Check conditions for an amicable pair:\n        # 1. sum1 must be greater than 1 (as sum_of_divisors(1) is 0)\n        # 2. sum1 must not be equal to num (to exclude perfect numbers)\n        # 3. sum1 must be within the upper_limit for its pair to be counted\n        if sum1 > 1 and sum1 != num and sum1 <= upper_limit:\n            sum2 = sum_of_divisors(sum1)\n            if sum2 == num:\n                # Found an amicable pair (num, sum1)\n                total_sum += num\n                total_sum += sum1\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(num)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(sum1)\n\n    return total_sum"}
