{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "# Helper function to find the first occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\ndef find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\n# Helper function to find the last occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\ndef find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the given element is the majority element in the sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = find_first_occurrence(arr, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = find_last_occurrence(arr, element)\n    \n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/230", "solution": "def replace_blank(input_string: str, replacement_char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces blank spaces in the input string with the specified character.\n    This function iterates through the string and builds a new string with replacements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char == ' ':\n            result.append(replacement_char)\n        else:\n            result.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result)"}
