{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def kadane_algorithm(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Core implementation of Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum subarray sum.\n    Handles arrays with all negative numbers by returning the largest negative sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0 \n    \n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    current_max = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        \n    return max_so_far\n\ndef calculate_prefix_suffix_sums(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum prefix sum, maximum suffix sum, and total sum of the array.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0, 0, 0\n\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    max_prefix = arr[0]\n    current_prefix_sum = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_prefix_sum += arr[i]\n        max_prefix = max(max_prefix, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    max_suffix = arr[n-1]\n    current_suffix_sum = arr[n-1]\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix_sum += arr[i]\n        max_suffix = max(max_suffix, current_suffix_sum)\n        \n    return max_prefix, max_suffix, total_sum\n\ndef calculate_repeated_max_sum(array: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles maximum subarray calculation logic for repeated arrays when k > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_single_kadane = kadane_algorithm(array)\n    max_prefix, max_suffix, total_sum = calculate_prefix_suffix_sums(array)\n\n    overall_max = max_single_kadane\n    \n    if total_sum > 0:\n        # If the total sum of the array is positive, it's beneficial to include (k-2) full arrays\n        # between the max suffix of the first array and max prefix of the last array.\n        # This formula also correctly handles k=2 where (k-2)*total_sum becomes 0.\n        spanning_sum = max_suffix + total_sum * (k - 2) + max_prefix\n        overall_max = max(overall_max, spanning_sum)\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is non-positive, including more than two arrays won't improve the sum\n        # for a spanning subarray. The maximum spanning sum will be found within the concatenation of two arrays.\n        spanning_sum_two_blocks = max_suffix + max_prefix\n        overall_max = max(overall_max, spanning_sum_two_blocks)\n\n    return overall_max\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array: list[int], k: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array \n    which is formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0 \n\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane_algorithm(array)\n    else:\n        return calculate_repeated_max_sum(array, k)"}
