{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, length, i, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from prefix until index i,\n    including the element at index k (where k > i).\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # dp[x] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index x\n    # considering elements from arr[0] up to arr[x].\n    dp = [0] * length\n\n    # Calculate dp values for elements up to index i\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        dp[j] = arr[j] # Initialize with the element itself, as it can be a subsequence of length 1\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[j] > arr[prev]:\n                # If arr[j] can extend an increasing subsequence ending at arr[prev]\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[prev] + arr[j])\n                \n    # Now, find the maximum sum from dp values that can precede arr[k].\n    # An element arr[j] (where j <= i) can precede arr[k] only if arr[j] < arr[k].\n    # Initialize with 0; this handles cases where no element from 0..i can precede arr[k].\n    max_sum_prefix_before_k = 0 \n    \n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_sum_prefix_before_k = max(max_sum_prefix_before_k, dp[j])\n            \n    # The total maximum sum is the sum of the best prefix subsequence and the mandatory element arr[k].\n    return max_sum_prefix_before_k + arr[k]"}
