{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "import functools\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given n using the recursive equation\n    f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n), with memoization.\n    \"\"\"\n    @functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n: int) -> int:\n        # Base case: for n <= 1, the maximum sum is n itself.\n        if current_n <= 1:\n            return current_n\n\n        # Calculate the sum of recursive calls using integer division.\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 2) +\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 3) +\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 4) +\n            _calculate_max_sum_recursive(current_n // 5)\n        )\n\n        # Return the maximum of the sum of parts or the current_n itself.\n        return max(sum_of_parts, current_n)\n\n    return _calculate_max_sum_recursive(n)"}
