{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "from typing import List\n\nclass DigitProcessor:\n    @staticmethod\n    def process_number(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Process a single number and return sum of its digits.\"\"\"\n        digits = DigitProcessor.extract_individual_digits(number)\n        return sum(digits)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def extract_individual_digits(number: int) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Extract individual digits from a number.\"\"\"\n        # Convert the number to a string to iterate through its digits.\n        # Assumes non-negative numbers based on the problem context.\n        return [int(digit) for digit in str(number)]\n\nclass ResultCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def accumulate_sum(digit_sums: List[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Accumulate digit sums into final result.\"\"\"\n        return sum(digit_sums)\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_input(input_list) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Validate input is a list of integers.\"\"\"\n        # Per constraints, no explicit isinstance() checks or exception raising.\n        # This method acts as a placeholder and always returns True.\n        return True\n\ndef sum_of_digits(input_list: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main function to compute sum of digits from list of integers.\"\"\"\n    # Validate the input list; this step is a placeholder as per design constraints.\n    if not InputValidator.validate_input(input_list):\n        return 0 # Should not be reached with valid input as per constraints.\n\n    individual_number_digit_sums = []\n    for number in input_list:\n        # Calculate the sum of digits for each number in the input list.\n        sum_of_current_number_digits = DigitProcessor.process_number(number)\n        individual_number_digit_sums.append(sum_of_current_number_digits)\n\n    # Accumulate all the individual sums of digits into a grand total.\n    total_sum_of_all_digits = ResultCalculator.accumulate_sum(individual_number_digit_sums)\n\n    return total_sum_of_all_digits"}
