{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(input_list: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list.\n    Filters out non-numeric values and returns the smallest numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_values = []\n    for item in input_list:\n        if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            numeric_values.append(item)\n\n    if not numeric_values:\n        # Per design, 'no isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases'\n        # The assert in the prompt implies there will always be a numeric value\n        # to find if the list is like the example. If no numeric values,\n        # the behavior is undefined by the prompt. Assuming built-in min\n        # will handle an empty list if it's the only option.\n        # For the given example, it will always return 2.\n        # However, the design context specifies \"Raises: ValueError: If no numeric values found in the list\".\n        # This is a contradiction. Given \"DO NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\",\n        # the safest path is to rely on Python's built-in min behavior for an empty list,\n        # which is to raise a ValueError itself.\n        pass # The min() function will raise ValueError if numeric_values is empty.\n\n    return min(numeric_values)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef min_product_tuple(tuples_list: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]) -> Union[int, float, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the minimum product from pairs of tuples within a given list.\n\n    Args:\n        tuples_list (List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]):\n            List of tuples where each tuple contains exactly two numeric elements\n\n    Returns:\n        Union[int, float, None]: Minimum product value, or None for empty list\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuples_list:\n        return None\n\n    min_product = tuples_list[0][0] * tuples_list[0][1]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(tuples_list)):\n        current_product = tuples_list[i][0] * tuples_list[i][1]\n        if current_product < min_product:\n            min_product = current_product\n\n    return min_product"}
