{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n    This handles positive, negative, and zero integers by considering products\n    of the two smallest and two largest numbers after sorting.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        # According to the problem constraints and assertion, arr will have at least 2 elements.\n        # This case is included for robustness, though not strictly required by design.\n        return None \n\n    # Sort the array to easily identify the smallest and largest numbers.\n    arr.sort()\n\n    # The maximum product can either be from the two largest numbers\n    # or from the two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    product_of_smallest_two = arr[0] * arr[1]\n    product_of_largest_two = arr[-1] * arr[-2]\n\n    if product_of_smallest_two > product_of_largest_two:\n        return (arr[0], arr[1])\n    else:\n        return (arr[-2], arr[-1])"}
