mbination + [element])\n        result.extend(new_combinations_for_element)\n    \n    # The assert's order for the main list of combinations is not strictly length then lexicographical\n    # for the entire list but rather an emergent order from how elements are added.\n    # The above reversal and extension directly matches the example output's generation logic.\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/459", "solution": "def _is_uppercase(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if character is uppercase letter.\"\"\"\n    return char.isupper()\n\ndef _build_result(chars: list) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Build result string from character list.\"\"\"\n    return \"\".join(chars)\n\ndef remove_uppercase(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove all contiguous uppercase substrings from the input string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to process\n\n    Returns:\n        str: String with uppercase substrings removed\n\n    Time Complexity: O(n) where n is the length of input string\n    \"\"\"\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if not _is_uppercase(char):\n            result_chars.append(char)\n    return _build_result(result_chars)"}
