{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "def extract_values(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all text values enclosed in double quotation marks from a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    extracted_values = []\n    n = len(input_string)\n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        if input_string[i] == '\"':\n            start_quote_index = i\n            # Search for the closing quote\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < n and input_string[j] != '\"':\n                j += 1\n            \n            if j < n and input_string[j] == '\"':\n                # Found a valid closing quote, extract content\n                extracted_values.append(input_string[start_quote_index + 1 : j])\n                i = j + 1  # Continue search after the closing quote\n            else:\n                # Malformed quote: opening quote without a closing one.\n                # Skip this opening quote and continue searching from the next character.\n                i = start_quote_index + 1\n        else:\n            i += 1  # Move to the next character if not a quote\n    return extracted_values"}
