{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "def sort_by_price(items):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of item dictionaries by their 'price' in descending order.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(items, key=lambda item: item['price'], reverse=True)\n\ndef select_top_n(sorted_items, n):\n    \"\"\"Selects the first n items from a pre-sorted list.\"\"\"\n    return sorted_items[:n]\n\ndef expensive_items(dataset, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n most expensive items in a given dataset.\n    Returns a list of dictionaries, sorted by price in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_data = sort_by_price(dataset)\n    top_n_items = select_top_n(sorted_data, n)\n    return top_n_items"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\n\ndef perfect_squares(start: int, end: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds perfect squares within a given range [start, end], inclusive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if end < start:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    \n    # Determine the smallest integer root whose square is >= start.\n    # We take max(0, start) to handle negative or zero 'start' values correctly for non-negative squares.\n    current_root = math.isqrt(max(0, start))\n    \n    # Adjust current_root if its square is still less than 'start'.\n    # Example: if start=2, isqrt(2)=1, but 1*1=1 < 2, so the next root (2) is needed.\n    if current_root * current_root < start:\n        current_root += 1\n\n    # Iterate through potential roots, calculating their squares.\n    while True:\n        square = current_root * current_root\n        if square > end:\n            break\n        result.append(square)\n        current_root += 1\n        \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/591", "solution": "def swap_List(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Interchanges the first and last elements in a list, returning a new list.\n    Handles lists of any length while preserving middle elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(input_list)\n    \n    return [input_list[-1]] + input_list[1:-1] + [input_list[0]]"}
