{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(limit: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all Ludic numbers less than or equal to the given limit using a sieve process.\n    \"\"\"\n    if limit <= 0:\n        return []\n    if limit == 1:\n        return [1]\n\n    # Initialize a list of candidate numbers from 1 up to the limit.\n    candidates = list(range(1, limit + 1))\n    ludic_numbers = []\n\n    while candidates:\n        # The first number in the candidates list is the next Ludic number.\n        ludic_num = candidates.pop(0)\n        ludic_numbers.append(ludic_num)\n\n        # If there are no more candidates, we are done.\n        if not candidates:\n            break\n        \n        # The sieve step: remove every `ludic_num`-th element from the remaining candidates.\n        # The rule for `ludic_num = 1` means only 1 itself is removed (already done by pop(0)).\n        if ludic_num == 1:\n            continue\n\n        new_candidates = []\n        count = 0  # This tracks the ordinal position in the current `candidates` list.\n        for i in range(len(candidates)):\n            count += 1\n            if count == ludic_num:\n                # If it's the `ludic_num`-th element, skip it (do not add to new_candidates)\n                count = 0  # Reset count for the next `ludic_num`-block of elements\n            else:\n                new_candidates.append(candidates[i])\n        candidates = new_candidates\n        \n    return ludic_numbers"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using a dynamic programming approach\n    based on the Bell triangle.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a 2D DP table to store Bell triangle values.\n    # dp[i][j] will store the j-th element of the i-th row of the Bell triangle.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # The first Bell number (B_0) is 1.\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle row by row.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row.\n        dp[i][0] = dp[i - 1][i - 1]\n        # Fill the rest of the elements in the current row.\n        # Each element is the sum of the element to its left and the element diagonally above it.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + dp[i][j - 1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (dp[n][0]).\n    return dp[n][0]"}
