{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It uses a binary search approach to find the two middle elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _find_kth_element(arr1: list, arr2: list, k: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper to find the k-th smallest element (1-indexed) in two sorted arrays.\n        This function assumes arr1 is not longer than arr2 for simpler logic.\n        \"\"\"\n        m, n = len(arr1), len(arr2)\n\n        if m > n:\n            return _find_kth_element(arr2, arr1, k)\n\n        low = max(0, k - n)\n        high = min(m, k)\n\n        while low <= high:\n            i = low + (high - low) // 2\n            j = k - i\n\n            L1 = arr1[i-1] if i > 0 else -float('inf')\n            R1 = arr1[i] if i < m else float('inf')\n            L2 = arr2[j-1] if j > 0 else -float('inf')\n            R2 = arr2[j] if j < n else float('inf')\n\n            if L1 <= R2 and L2 <= R1:\n                return float(max(L1, L2))\n            elif L1 > R2:\n                high = i - 1\n            else: # L2 > R1\n                low = i + 1\n        return -1.0 # Should not be reached with valid inputs\n\n    # The median for an even total number of elements (2 * size) is the average\n    # of the (size)-th and (size + 1)-th smallest elements.\n    k1_element = _find_kth_element(list1, list2, size)\n    k2_element = _find_kth_element(list1, list2, size + 1)\n    \n    return (k1_element + k2_element) / 2.0"}
