{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Helper function to maintain heap property\n    def heapify(arr, n, i):\n        largest = i\n        left = 2 * i + 1\n        right = 2 * i + 2\n\n        if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n            heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\n    # Helper function to build a max heap\n    def build_max_heap(arr):\n        for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n            heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # Build a max heap\n    build_max_heap(arr)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Swap root with current last element\n        heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Heapify the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\n\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index rounded to the next integer, given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    The calculation uses the standard wind chill formula: WCI = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate V to the power of 0.16 for the formula\n    v_power_016 = wind_velocity ** 0.16\n\n    # Apply the wind chill formula\n    wind_chill_index_float = (13.12 + \n                              (0.6215 * temperature) - \n                              (11.37 * v_power_016) + \n                              (0.3965 * temperature * v_power_016))\n\n    # Round the result to the next integer (ceiling)\n    return math.ceil(wind_chill_index_float)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "def move_zero(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Moves all zeroes to the end of the given list while preserving\n    the relative order of non-zero elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_zeros = []\n    zero_count = 0\n    for x in input_list:\n        if x != 0:\n            non_zeros.append(x)\n        else:\n            zero_count += 1\n    non_zeros.extend([0] * zero_count)\n    return non_zeros"}
