{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def calculate_triangular_number(k):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the kth triangular number using the formula k*(k+1)/2.\"\"\"\n    return k * (k + 1) // 2\n\ndef count_digits(number):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of digits in a given integer by converting it to a string.\"\"\"\n    return len(str(number))\n\ndef validate_input(n):\n    \"\"\"Validates that the input n is a positive integer, returning True if valid.\"\"\"\n    return n > 0\n\ndef find_Index(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with exactly n digits.\n    It iteratively calculates triangular numbers until the digit count matches n.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The design suggests input validation. Based on problem constraints, n is assumed positive.\n    # if not validate_input(n):\n    #     # Error handling for invalid n is omitted as per problem constraints.\n    #     pass\n\n    k = 1  # Start with the first triangular number index (T_1 = 1)\n\n    while True:\n        triangular_num = calculate_triangular_number(k)\n        digit_count = count_digits(triangular_num)\n\n        if digit_count == n:\n            return k\n        \n        k += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(array: list, target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the left insertion point for a specified value in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index where the target should be inserted to maintain sorted order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0\n\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
