{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions.\n    A new list is returned without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(lst)\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    if effective_positions == 0:\n        return list(lst)  # Return a copy if no rotation is needed\n\n    # Split the list into two parts and concatenate them in reverse order\n    # The last 'effective_positions' elements go to the beginning\n    # The remaining 'n - effective_positions' elements follow\n    return lst[-effective_positions:] + lst[:-effective_positions]"}
