{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum, endnum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers in a range where each number is divisible by all its constituent digits.\n    Numbers containing the digit 0 are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    def extract_digits(number):\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a number.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        temp_num = abs(number)\n        while temp_num > 0:\n            digits.append(temp_num % 10)\n            temp_num //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]\n\n    def contains_zero(number):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number contains the digit zero.\"\"\"\n        return '0' in str(number)\n\n    def is_divisible_by_all_digits(number):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is divisible by all its digits.\"\"\"\n        digits = extract_digits(number)\n        for digit in digits:\n            if digit == 0 or number % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if num == 0:  # 0 is a special case, typically not included in such problems or handled as per specific rules\n            continue\n        if not contains_zero(num) and is_divisible_by_all_digits(num):\n            result.append(num)\n    return result"}
