{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "def is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string is a decimal number with exactly 2 decimal places.\n    Handles positive numbers in XXX.XX format.\n    \"\"\"\n    # A valid decimal must contain exactly one decimal point.\n    if input_string.count('.') != 1:\n        return False\n\n    # Split the string into integer and fractional parts.\n    integer_part, fractional_part = input_string.split('.')\n\n    # The integer part must not be empty and must consist solely of digits.\n    # This also implicitly handles leading '+' or '-' as isdigit() would return False.\n    if not integer_part or not integer_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    # The fractional part must have exactly two characters and consist solely of digits.\n    if len(fractional_part) != 2 or not fractional_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef _is_reverse(str1: str, str2: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if two strings are exact reverses of each other.\n    Performs case-sensitive string comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    return str1 == str2[::-1]\n\ndef _is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string is a palindrome.\n    Compares the string with its reverse.\n    \"\"\"\n    return s == s[::-1]\n\ndef count_reverse_pairs(strings: List[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of strings in the given list where one string is the reverse of another,\n    excluding pairs where either string is a palindrome.\n    \"\"\"\n    reverse_pair_count = 0\n    num_strings = len(strings)\n\n    for i in range(num_strings):\n        for j in range(i + 1, num_strings):\n            s1 = strings[i]\n            s2 = strings[j]\n\n            # Check if s2 is the reverse of s1\n            if _is_reverse(s1, s2):\n                # Only count the pair if s1 (and consequently s2, given they are reverses)\n                # is not a palindrome, as per the requirement.\n                if not _is_palindrome(s1):\n                    reverse_pair_count += 1\n    return reverse_pair_count"}
