{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, target: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position (index) of an element in a sorted array.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n\n        if array[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Store this as a potential answer\n            low = mid + 1 # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1 # Target is in the right half\n        else: # array[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1 # Target is in the left half\n    \n    return result"}
