{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are considered positive integers (1, 2, 3, ...).\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Natural numbers typically start from 1. Ensure the loop starts from at least 1.\n    start = max(1, l)\n\n    # Iterate through the numbers in the range [start, r]\n    for num in range(start, r + 1):\n        if num % 2 != 0:  # Check if the current number is odd\n            total_sum += num\n            \n    return total_sum"}
